          "en": "I took it up and glanced at it. “Mr. Victor Hatherley, hydraulic engineer, 16A, Victoria Street (3rd floor).” That was the name, style, and abode of my morning visitor. “I regret that I have kept you waiting,” said I, sitting down in my library-chair. “You are fresh from a night journey, I understand, which is in itself a monotonous occupation.”",
          "es": "La tomé y eché un vistazo. \"Sr. Victor Hatherley, ingeniero hidráulico, 16A, Victoria Street (3ª planta).\" Ese era el nombre, título y domicilio de mi visitante matutino. \"Lamento haberlo tenido esperando,\" dije, sentándome en mi sillón de consultorio. \"Viene de un viaje nocturno, entiendo, que es en sí una ocupación monótona.\""
